  "description": "Behringer UB-1 MICRO analog-modelled mini synthesizer: every controller of its quick start guide's MIDI table, with the values it prints.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "type": "manual",
      "title": "UB-1 MICRO Quick Start Guide",
      "notes": "MIDI controller table (pages 40, 41) read by tools/profiles/behringer/read-behringer-cc.mjs from QSG_BE_0722-ABS_UB-1-MICRO_2025-04-02_Rev.0.pdf (sha256 b2b6970637c1bffff7c2bc0a7d141ad3e553bb68be00142a84f497afecdf95a9), https://cdn-media.empowertribe.com/e2441bd3e41d45f89d09044dddb6f26c/QSG_BE_0722-ABS_UB-1-MICRO_2025-04-02_Rev.0.pdf. Not yet checked against the instrument itself."
    }
  ],
  "testedWith": [],
  "authoringNotes": [
    "Generated by tools/profiles/behringer/make-profiles.mjs; edit the layout in tools/profiles/behringer/synths/, not this file.",
    "Every parameter is a row of the guide's MIDI controller table, with its printed name, sent as a control change on the channel variable. Nothing here has been sent to a real instrument yet.",
    "Ranges are as printed (`0 - 99`): the guide does not say whether a range is the controller's values or what the panel shows for them.",
    "Rows the guide prints wrongly, given by the layout: CC 25 (printed 0-32 off, 32-63 sawtooth: 0-31), CC 106 (printed 86-106 …, 87-127: 107-127).",
    "Left out, controllers that change the instrument's MIDI channels: CC 14 MIDI Tx Channel, CC 15 MIDI Rx Channel."
  ],
